{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And you shall return to HaShem your Elohim, and you shall obey His voice</b>. This too is an allusion to the redemption of Babylon: that they returned to HaShem and confessed before Him, and they obeyed the voice of the prophets whom He raised up for them. Therefore He promised them that He would not destroy them and would not forget the covenant of their fathers, as He said (Leviticus 26:42), \"And I will remember My covenant with Jacob,\" etc. And at the end of the book He will allude to the future redemption, as I explained (there in verse 16), and we shall mention it again, with the help of Heaven (Ramban on Deuteronomy 28:42)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The phrase 'העזרתי' appears as 'בע\"ה' (בעזרת השם, 'with the help of Heaven') resolved by context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:20.954118649Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}